 "capsule": "Lu (魯) was a Zhou dynasty vassal state in southwestern Shandong, founded around 1042 BCE for Boqin, son of the Duke of Zhou, with its capital at Qufu. Renowned above all as the home state of Confucius, Lu's ducal reign-years supplied the chronological spine of the Spring and Autumn Annals, the text that gave the era its name. Lu persisted as a minor power for roughly eight centuries before Chu conquered it in 256 BCE; its last duke, Duke Qing, died as a commoner around 249 BCE.",
